IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`
IMPORT `earn-kernel`

§ `Citi ThankYou Points / Citi Miles / Cash Back / SMRT$ / Citi M1 Rebate / Cash Rebate Exclusion Terms and Conditions`

-- ===========================================================================
-- DOCUMENT. citi-rewards-exclusion-list, "Updated November 2024. With effect
-- from 16 December 2024." (Citibank Singapore Ltd), cl.1-6.
-- INCORPORATED BY REFERENCE by Citi Rewards 10X cl.5(xii) ("a merchant that
-- has been excluded by the bank, as set out in www.citibank.com.sg/rwdexcl")
-- and by the PremierMiles Program T&C cl.3.3(xii). This module encodes the
-- list once; citi-10x.l4 and citi-premiermiles.l4 call it.
--
-- WHAT THE DOCUMENT SAYS, in the shape it says it.
--   cl.1  lists the Cards covered (here: Citi PremierMiles Card, Citi Rewards
--         Card) and says Citibank may exclude others "with notice".
--   cl.2  no reward "will be awarded to the above Cards with transactions made
--         in the following Merchant Category Codes", under five headings, each
--         with a range in parentheses ("Quasi Cash / Financial Services (MCC
--         6529-6540), such as but not limited to:") and then the codes.
--   cl.3  no reward for transactions "with the following merchants and/or
--         bearing the following merchant descriptions", and footnote 2 extends
--         it to "any combination, permutation or derivation ... whether in
--         whole or in part".
--   cl.4  "the above excluded Merchant Category Codes ('MCC') and the above
--         excluded merchant list is not exhaustive and may be updated".
--
-- THE OPEN READING (fork F-citi-excl-ranges). The five headings give ranges
-- (6529-6540, 8211-8299, 8062 and 8651-8661, 9000-9999) and each says "such as
-- but not limited to". Reading 1: only the codes the table lists are excluded.
-- Reading 2: every code inside a named range is excluded. The text of the
-- table lists, e.g., 6529, 6530, 6534 and 6540 inside 6529-6540 and omits
-- 6531-6533 and 6535-6539. The module takes Reading 1 as the answer and
-- reports Reading 2 as a named condition whenever the two differ. ASSUMED, NOT
-- RULED.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `cl.1 -- the Cards the list covers`

-- The list names, among others, "Citi PremierMiles Card" (cl.1(c)) and "Citi
-- Rewards Card" (cl.1(f)).
GIVEN c IS A Card
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Citi exclusion list covers` c MEANS
    c EQUALS `Citi PremierMiles Visa`
    OR c EQUALS `Citi PremierMiles Mastercard`
    OR c EQUALS `Citi Rewards Visa Signature`
    OR c EQUALS `Citi Rewards World Mastercard`


§§ `cl.2 -- the Merchant Category Codes that earn nothing`

-- Every code the table lists, in the table's order: Quasi Cash / Financial
-- Services (6529, 6530, 6534, 6540, 7349, 7511, 7523, 7800, 7995, 4829, 4900,
-- 5199, 5960, 6012, 6050, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6513), Education Institutions
-- (8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299, 8398), Professional Services and
-- Membership Organizations (8062, 8651, 8661), Government Services (9211,
-- 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405, 9754), Other Miscellaneous (5993).
-- The footnotes "*Not applicable for Citi Business Visa Card / Citi Corporate
-- Visa Card, Citi Purchasing Visa Card, Citi Travel Account Visa Card" (on
-- 4900) and "**Not applicable for Citi ULTIMA Card" (on 8062) concern cards
-- no module here covers.
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`the Citi excluded category codes` MEANS
    LIST 6529, 6530, 6534, 6540, 7349, 7511, 7523, 7800, 7995, 4829, 4900,
         5199, 5960, 6012, 6050, 6051, 6211, 6300, 6513,
         8211, 8220, 8241, 8244, 8249, 8299, 8398,
         8062, 8651, 8661,
         9211, 9222, 9223, 9311, 9399, 9402, 9405, 9754,
         5993

-- Reading 1: the table's own codes.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Citi table lists the code of` p MEANS
    `the code is among` p `the Citi excluded category codes`

-- Reading 2: the code lies inside a range a heading names.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Citi heading's range holds the code of` p MEANS
       `the code is from` p 6529 6540
    OR `the code is from` p 8211 8299
    OR `the code is from` p 8651 8661
    OR `the code is among` p (LIST 8062)
    OR `the code is from` p 9000 9999


§§ `cl.3 -- the merchant descriptions that earn nothing`

-- The twenty entries, folded to the counterparties they name: AXS, AMAZE* AXS,
-- BANC DE BINARY, BUS/MRT, AMAZE* BUS/MRT, EZ-link, AMAZE* EZ-link, OANDA ASIA
-- PAC, SAM, Saxo Cap Mkts Pte Ltd, SIMPLYGO*, SPL AUTO* / SPL ATU* / SPL
-- ONLINE*, SKYFX.COM, TL-ABT, TRANSIT, AMAZE* TRANSIT, Transit Link, Youtrip
-- Singapore SG. A bare "AMAZE" is NOT on the list; only Amaze combined with a
-- listed counterparty is, by the entries "AMAZE* AXS", "AMAZE* BUS/MRT",
-- "AMAZE* EZ-link" and "AMAZE* TRANSIT" and footnote 2's "combination".
GIVEN d IS A Descriptor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Citi list names the description` d MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `AXS`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Amaze with a transit or payment counterparty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `EZ-Link`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Transit Link`                                THEN TRUE
    WHEN `TRANSIT`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SimplyGo as a descriptor`                    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SPL AUTO or SPL ATU or SPL ONLINE`           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `TL-ABT`                                      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `BUS/MRT as a descriptor`                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Youtrip`                                     THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SAM`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `OANDA`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Saxo`                                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `SkyFX`                                       THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Banc de Binary`                              THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE                                               FALSE


§§ `Whether a purchase is excluded, and under which reading`

-- TRUE iff the table's own codes (Reading 1) or a listed description exclude it.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Citi exclusion list excludes` p MEANS
    `the Citi table lists the code of` p
    OR `the Citi list names the description` (p's descriptor)

-- TRUE iff only Reading 2 would exclude it: the code is inside a named range
-- but is not itself listed, and no description excludes it.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`only the Citi ranges would exclude` p MEANS
    `a Citi heading's range holds the code of` p
    AND NOT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` p


§§ `Illustrations -- the printed lists, one assertion per entry class`

-- cl.2: a code that is printed.
`a card payment at a school` MEANS
    Purchase WITH
        `amount in SGD`      IS 100
        `date charged`       IS Date 5 10 2026
        `date posted`        IS Date 6 10 2026
        `posting status`     IS `Posted to the account`
        `charge kind`        IS `Retail purchase`
        currency             IS `Singapore dollars`
        gateway              IS `A gateway in Singapore`
        `store location`     IS `A store in Singapore`
        presentation         IS `Card number entered online`
        `merchant indicator` IS `Flags online`
        merchant             IS `Another merchant`
        outlet               IS `An ordinary outlet`
        item                 IS `An ordinary item`
        mcc                  IS JUST 8211
        descriptor           IS `Another description`
        `later reversed`     IS FALSE

GIVEN code IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Purchase
`a purchase coded` code MEANS
    `recoded purchase` `a card payment at a school` code

#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` `a card payment at a school`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 5311))
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6529)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6530)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6534)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6540)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 7349)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 7511)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 7523)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 7800)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 7995)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 4829)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 4900)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 5199)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 5960)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6012)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6050)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6051)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6211)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6300)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6513)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 8398)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 8062)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 9311)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 9754)
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 5993)
#ASSERT `the Citi table lists the code of` (`a purchase coded` 8299)

-- Parking (7523) and Government (9399) are on the list; a clothing store
-- (5651), a bakery (5462) and a restaurant (5812) are not.
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 5651))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 5462))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 5812))

-- The open reading (F-citi-excl-ranges): 6531 is inside 6529-6540 and is not
-- printed; 8250 is inside 8211-8299 and is not printed; 9000 is inside
-- 9000-9999 and is not printed.
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi exclusion list excludes` (`a purchase coded` 6531))
#ASSERT `only the Citi ranges would exclude` (`a purchase coded` 6531)
#ASSERT `only the Citi ranges would exclude` (`a purchase coded` 8250)
#ASSERT `only the Citi ranges would exclude` (`a purchase coded` 9000)
#ASSERT NOT (`only the Citi ranges would exclude` (`a purchase coded` 8211))
#ASSERT NOT (`only the Citi ranges would exclude` (`a purchase coded` 5812))

-- cl.3: a description. "AMAZE* AXS" excludes; a bare "AMAZE" is not on this
-- list; "EZ-link", "SIMPLYGO*", "Youtrip" and "OANDA" are.
#ASSERT `the Citi list names the description` `AXS`
#ASSERT `the Citi list names the description` `Amaze with a transit or payment counterparty`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi list names the description` `Amaze`)
#ASSERT `the Citi list names the description` `EZ-Link`
#ASSERT `the Citi list names the description` `SimplyGo as a descriptor`
#ASSERT `the Citi list names the description` `Youtrip`
#ASSERT `the Citi list names the description` `OANDA`
#ASSERT `the Citi list names the description` `SPL AUTO or SPL ATU or SPL ONLINE`
#ASSERT `the Citi list names the description` `TL-ABT`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi list names the description` `IG Markets`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi list names the description` `ShopeePay`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi list names the description` `Another description`)

-- cl.1: coverage of the four Citi constructors held here, and of no other card.
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list covers` `Citi PremierMiles Visa`
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list covers` `Citi PremierMiles Mastercard`
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list covers` `Citi Rewards Visa Signature`
#ASSERT `the Citi exclusion list covers` `Citi Rewards World Mastercard`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Citi exclusion list covers` `UOB PRVI Miles Visa`)
